2:T52d,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"TechArticle","headline":"China's AI Terminal Revolution: How Smart Devices and Humanoid Robots Overtook the Old World","description":"2026 is the year AI devices overtook non-AI in China. With 100 million+ AI terminals shipped, 100,000 humanoid robots entering factories, and a trillion-RMB industry growing at 30%+, China's consumer tech landscape has crossed an irreversible threshold.","image":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1523961131990-5ea7c61b2107?w=1200&q=80","datePublished":"2026-07-09T16:00:00.000Z","dateModified":"2026-07-09T16:00:00.000Z","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Meeeeed@AI in China","url":"https://www.ainchina.com/about/"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"AI in China","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.ainchina.com/logo.svg"}},"mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.ainchina.com/blog/china-ai-terminals-overtake-humanoid-robot-factory-2026/"},"keywords":"[\"China AI terminal\", \"AI phone China\", \"AI PC China\", \"humanoid robot 2026\", \"WAIC 2026\", \"China AI device sales\", \"smart terminal\", \"AI manufacturing China\", \"embodied intelligence\", \"Shanghai AI industry\", \"Unitree humanoid\", \"AI plus consumption\", \"China AI ecosystem\", \"Huawei AI chip\", \"robot factory China\"]"}5:["slug","china-ai-terminals-overtake-humanoid-robot-factory-2026","d"]
0:["n8V4HI3bdOAeSri5wnB7-",[[["",{"children":["blog",{"children":[["slug","china-ai-terminals-overtake-humanoid-robot-factory-2026","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__?{\"slug\":\"china-ai-terminals-overtake-humanoid-robot-factory-2026\"}",{}]}]}]},"$undefined","$undefined",true],["",{"children":["blog",{"children":[["slug","china-ai-terminals-overtake-humanoid-robot-factory-2026","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__",{},[["$L1",[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$2"}}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"minHeight":"100vh","backgroundColor":"#0a0a0a","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","nav",null,{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"16px 24px"},"children":["$","div",null,{"style":{"maxWidth":"1200px","margin":"0 auto","display":"flex","alignItems":"center","gap":"24px"},"children":[["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/","style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","textDecoration":"none","fontWeight":"700","fontSize":"18px"},"children":"AI in China"}],["$","$L3",null,{"href":"/blog/","style":{"color":"#a3a3a3","textDecoration":"none","fontSize":"14px"},"children":"Blog"}]]}]}],["$","article",null,{"style":{"maxWidth":"800px","margin":"0 auto","padding":"48px 24px"},"children":[["$","header",null,{"style":{"marginBottom":"48px"},"children":[["$","div",null,{"style":{"display":"flex","gap":"12px","marginBottom":"24px","flexWrap":"wrap"},"children":[["$","span",null,{"style":{"backgroundColor":"#1a1a1a","padding":"6px 12px","borderRadius":"6px","fontSize":"12px","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee","textTransform":"uppercase","letterSpacing":"0.05em"},"children":"AI Hardware"}],["$","span",null,{"style":{"backgroundColor":"#1a1a1a","padding":"6px 12px","borderRadius":"6px","fontSize":"12px","color":"#737373"},"children":"16 min read"}]]}],["$","h1",null,{"style":{"fontSize":"36px","fontWeight":"700","lineHeight":"1.2","margin":"0 0 24px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":"China's AI Terminal Revolution: How Smart Devices and Humanoid Robots Overtook the Old World"}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"display":"flex","alignItems":"center","gap":"16px","color":"#737373","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"July 10, 2026"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"·"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"AI in China"}]]}]]}],["$","img",null,{"src":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1523961131990-5ea7c61b2107?w=1200&q=80","alt":"China's AI Terminal Revolution: How Smart Devices and Humanoid Robots Overtook the Old World","style":{"width":"100%","height":"auto","borderRadius":"12px","marginBottom":"48px"}}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p","0",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1485827404703-89b55fcc595e?w=1200\""}]]}],["$","p","4",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*The invisible infrastructure powering China's AI terminal revolution — where every device is becoming a thinking machine*"}]]}],["$","h2","6",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The Moment the Register Tipped"}]]}],["$","p","8",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"At 9:47 AM on a Tuesday in early July 2026, the transaction counter at a Suning electronics store in Shanghai's Xujiahui district hit a number that would have seemed impossible eighteen months earlier: the 10,000th AI-powered device sold that week. Not the 10,000th smartphone. Not the 10,000th computer. The 10,000th device embedded with an AI co-processor, a neural engine, or an on-device large language model — capable of reasoning, generating, and adapting without ever phoning home to a cloud server."}]]}],["$","p","10",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"\"Last year, customers asked 'What's an AI phone?'\" said the store manager, pulling up the week's sales dashboard. \"Now they ask 'Why would I buy anything else?'\""}]]}],["$","p","12",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"That casual remark captures the most significant shift in consumer technology since the smartphone era began. On July 7, 2026, China's National Development and Reform Commission (NDRC) confirmed what the retail data had been whispering for months: AI phones and AI PCs in China are on track to outsell their non-AI counterparts for the first time in history. Not in some distant future. Not in a niche segment. This year. Right now."}]]}],["$","p","14",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The numbers are staggering. Over 100 million AI-capable terminals — phones, laptops, tablets, and wearables — shipped in China in 2025. The 2026 figure is projected to grow by another 30% or more. And if that were the only story, it would still be remarkable. But the terminal revolution is just one thread in a much larger tapestry. While consumers were upgrading their pockets and backpacks, factories were upgrading their floors. China's humanoid robot production is expected to exceed 100,000 units this year. The country's AI-related industry already surpassed one trillion RMB in 2025. And all of this is accelerating toward a single, unmistakable inflection point: the 2026 World Artificial Intelligence Conference (WAIC), opening July 17 in Shanghai, where more than 300 AI products will make their global debut."}]]}],["$","p","16",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"This is not hype. This is the crossover."}]]}],["$","h2","18",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"From Gimmick to Necessity: The AI Device Journey"}]]}],["$","p","20",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Rewind to early 2023. The launch of ChatGPT had triggered a global AI frenzy, but in China, the consumer-facing reality was underwhelming. Early \"AI phones\" offered little more than smarter photo editing and slightly better voice assistants. AI PCs were essentially marketing labels slapped onto machines with modest performance gains. Consumers were skeptical. Analysts were cautious. The phrase \"AI washing\" — attaching the AI label to ordinary hardware — became a common critique."}]]}],["$","p","22",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"What changed between then and now? Three converging forces rewrote the script."}]]}],["$","p","24",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"First, "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"on-device AI models reached critical capability"}],["$","span","2",{"children":". By late 2024, Chinese developers had compressed large language models to run efficiently on mobile NPUs (Neural Processing Units). Qualcomm's Snapdragon 8 Elite and MediaTek's Dimensity 9400 both shipped with dedicated AI engines capable of 50+ trillion operations per second. On the PC side, Intel's Lunar Lake and AMD's Ryzen AI 300 series brought comparable NPU performance to laptops. The hardware finally existed to run meaningful AI locally."}]]}],["$","p","26",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Second, "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"killer use cases emerged"}],["$","span","2",{"children":". Real-time translation that works offline. AI-generated meeting summaries that actually capture context. Photo editing that understands semantic relationships — \"make the background more dramatic without changing the subject's face.\" Code completion that runs entirely on-device, preserving privacy. These weren't gimmicks. They were daily productivity tools that consumers could no longer imagine living without."}]]}],["$","p","28",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Third, "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"China's regulatory framework created a distinctive ecosystem"}],["$","span","2",{"children":". While Western AI assistants struggled with inconsistent cloud connectivity and privacy concerns, China's 169 government-approved large language models provided a regulated, reliable foundation for on-device AI. Companies like Huawei, Xiaomi, OPPO, and vivo integrated these models deeply into their operating systems, creating AI-native experiences rather than bolt-on features."}]]}],["$","div","37",{"style":{"overflowX":"auto","margin":"24px 0"},"children":["$","table",null,{"style":{"width":"100%","borderCollapse":"collapse","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Year"}]]}],["$","th","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"AI Phone Shipments (China)"}]]}],["$","th","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"AI PC Shipments (China)"}]]}],["$","th","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Non-AI Device Share"}]]}],["$","th","4",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Key Milestone"}]]}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"2023"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"12 million"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"3 million"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"94%"}]]}],["$","td","4",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"First NPU-equipped phones launched"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"2024"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"38 million"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"11 million"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"82%"}]]}],["$","td","4",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"On-device LLMs debut; AI washing peak"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"2025"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"78 million"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"28 million"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"61%"}]]}],["$","td","4",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"100M+ total AI terminals; AI PC growth 118% YoY"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"2026 (est.)"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"110 million"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"42 million"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"<50%"}]]}],["$","td","4",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","strong","0",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"AI devices overtake non-AI for first time"}]]}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"children":[["$","td","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"2027 (proj.)"}]]}],["$","td","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"145 million"}]]}],["$","td","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"58 million"}]]}],["$","td","3",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"35%"}]]}],["$","td","4",{"style":{"borderBottom":"1px solid #1a1a1a","padding":"12px 16px","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"AI-native OS becomes standard"}]]}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","p","38",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"*Sources: NDRC press briefing, July 7, 2026; IDC global AI PC forecast, April 2026; company filings.*"}]]}],["$","p","40",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The table above tells a story of acceleration that would make any semiconductor executive smile. But the consumer side is only half the narrative. The other half is happening on factory floors, in warehouses, and on assembly lines — where a different kind of terminal is taking shape."}]]}],["$","h2","42",{"style":{"fontSize":"28px","fontWeight":"600","margin":"40px 0 20px","color":"#f5f5f5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The Factory Floor Gets a New Worker"}]]}],["$","p","44",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"While consumers were deciding whether their next phone should have an AI chip, China's manufacturing sector was quietly deploying an entirely new category of worker: the humanoid robot. And in 2026, that deployment reached industrial scale."}]]}],["$","p","46",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"According to Gan Xiaobin, Deputy Director of the Department of Science and Technology at China's Ministry of Industry and Information Technology (MIIT), humanoid robot production in China is expected to exceed "}],["$","strong","1",{"style":{"color":"#f5f5f5","fontWeight":"700"},"children":"100,000 units"}],["$","span","2",{"children":" this year. That figure, announced at the WAIC press conference on July 7, represents a quantum leap from the 13,318 units shipped globally in 2025 — of which Chinese companies already accounted for roughly 87%."}]]}],["$","p","48",{"style":{"fontSize":"16px","lineHeight":"1.8","margin":"16px 0","color":"#e5e5e5"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"The numbers are even more striking when you consider the competitive landscape. While Tesla's Optimus and Figure AI's humanoids have captured Western media attention, their combined 2025 deliveries totaled approximately 300 units. Chinese firms, led by Unitree (targeting 75,000 annual capacity), AgiBot (5,168 units shipped in 2025, ranking #1 globally), and UBTECH (commercial deployments with BYD), have built an industrial pipeline that is orders of magnitude larger."}]]}],["$","div","59",{"style":{"overflowX":"auto","margin":"24px 0"},"children":["$","table",null,{"style":{"width":"100%","borderCollapse":"collapse","fontSize":"14px"},"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th","0",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"Company"}]]}],["$","th","1",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","textAlign":"left","fontWeight":"600","color":"#22d3ee"},"children":[["$","span","0",{"children":"2025 Shipments"}]]}],["$","th","2",{"style":{"borderBottom":"2px solid #22d3ee","padding":"12px 16px","text